  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution to Caritas Haiti Hurricane Matthew Rapid Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hurricane Matthew formed on September 29, 2016 in the Atlantic Ocean. On the night of 3 to 4 October 2016 and during the October 4, he hit the southern coast of Grand Anse, Nippes, South East, West, Artibonite and Northwest with a speed of 220 km/h and was ranked a level 4 Hurricane. 05 Oct 2016, the red alert was lifted because Matthew has left Haiti&apos;s ratings headed for the Bahamas. The information thus collected are beginning to highlight the intensity of damage. There would also 108 dead according to official data at this time.

This Rapid Response is to support 2,700 families (13,500 people) affected by Hurricane Matthew in the following areas: a) Acquisition and distribution of 2,700 food kits 2) awareness of the spread of infectious diseases and 3) distribution of 2,700 kits hygiene.</narrative>
  </description>
